#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/albion.adoc:195
msgid ""
"_The Druid harnesses the power of the weather to attack his enemies with "
"enormous hailstones._"
msgstr ""
"_Le Druide exploite la puissance météorologique pour attaquer ses ennemis "
"avec d'énormes grêlons._"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/albion.adoc:200
msgid ""
"The Druid targets a single enemy unit within range and that he can see. This "
"has the effect of three shooting attacks except that it ignores any armour "
"save the target may have. The target unit may be driven back in the same way "
"as for shooting."
msgstr ""
"Le Druide cible une unité ennemie à portée qu’il peut voir. Le sort est "
"traité comme 3 attaques de tir ordinaires, si ce n’est que l’armure de la "
"cible est ignorée (elle compte comme n’ayant pas d’Armure). Une unité peut "
"être repoussée par la Tempête de Grêle comme par une attaque de tir normale."

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/albion.adoc:202
#, no-wrap
msgid "Mists of Albion"
msgstr "Brumes d’Albion"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/albion.adoc:209
msgid ""
"_The Druid breathes out some of the mystical mist that surrounds his "
"enigmatic homeland and envelopes his compatriots, making them hard to target "
"by enemy troops._"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/albion.adoc:215
msgid ""
"This spell may be cast upon a single unengaged friendly Infantry unit within "
"range, regardless of whether the caster can see them or not. The spell lasts "
"until the start of the caster’s next turn, or until the target unit moves in "
"any way. The target Infantry unit counts as Defended, even if in the open "
"terrain."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/albion.adoc:217
#, no-wrap
msgid "Summon Fenbeast"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/albion.adoc:220
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/beastmen.adoc:252
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/chaos-dwarfs.adoc:248
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/daemons.adoc:249
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/high-elves.adoc:177
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/skaven.adoc:312
msgid "[.cost]#6+ to cast# [.points]#Range 30cm#"
msgstr "[.cost]#6+ pour lancer# [.points]#Portée 30cm#"

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/albion.adoc:224
msgid ""
"_The Druid performs one of the most arcane rituals known to his order, using "
"his power over the elements to bind together the horrific creature known as "
"the Fenbeast._"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/albion.adoc:227
msgid ""
"The Druid summons forth a Fenbeast. Once summoned, the Fenbeast is under the "
"control of the summoning player."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/albion.adoc:235
msgid ""
"Since it is summoned in the Shooting phase it cannot be given orders until "
"the following turn. It may be summoned into contact with an enemy unit only "
"if that unit is already in combat. It may be removed from play if destroyed "
"(like any other unit) or if the loss of a Druid character reduces the number "
"of Druids to less than the number of Fenbeasts – the owning player chooses a "
"Fenbeast and removes it from play."
msgstr ""

#.  Summoned
#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/albion.adoc:240
msgid ""
"Summoned Fenbeast units do not influence army withdrawal calculations in any "
"way and do not have a points value."
msgstr ""

#.  Paragraphs added.
#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/albion.adoc:246
msgid ""
"Fenbeasts may only be given orders by Druids. Fenbeasts may not be brigaded "
"with other troops, not even other Fenbeasts. An army cannot have more "
"summoned Fenbeasts in play than it has Druids."
msgstr ""
